# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values. .env is gitignored - it never gets committed.
#
# NORMAL SETUP: Vimeo publishing doesn't need any of this file - open the app itself and use the
# "Set up Vimeo publishing…" panel (next to the save-path fields), which walks through it and
# saves everything to data/vimeo-app-config.json instead. The VIMEO_* variables below are an
# advanced/optional override for anyone who'd rather manage it as env vars (e.g. a scripted
# install) - if set, they take priority over the in-app panel and lock its fields. Leave them all
# blank unless you specifically want that.
#
# Two ways to connect Vimeo this way - use ONE of them, not both:
#  1. VIMEO_ACCESS_TOKEN alone: a personal access token, generated by hand once and pasted in.
#     Works immediately, no further setup, but has to be copied into .env on every machine by hand.
#  2. VIMEO_CLIENT_ID + VIMEO_CLIENT_SECRET: identifies a Vimeo API app (same values shown on the
#     app's page where a personal access token would otherwise be generated) - same values the
#     in-app setup panel would otherwise ask for and save on its own.
# Requires a Vimeo plan that supports API uploads either way (Pro/Business/Premium - not free).

# Option 1: a personal access token from https://developer.vimeo.com/apps - needs the public,
# private, upload, edit, and interact scopes.
VIMEO_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# Option 2: the Client Identifier and Client Secret from the same app page as above - leave
# VIMEO_ACCESS_TOKEN blank to use this instead, then click "Connect Vimeo" in the app.
VIMEO_CLIENT_ID=
VIMEO_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Only needed if the app isn't reachable at http://localhost:3000 (e.g. a different port) - must
# exactly match the redirect URI registered with the Vimeo app. Only relevant to option 2.
VIMEO_REDIRECT_URI=

# Comma-separated showcase (album) IDs every published video gets added to, e.g. the current
# year's sermons, the current sermon series, and the all-sermons showcase. Find an ID in the
# showcase's URL: vimeo.com/showcase/XXXXXXX. Update this when the year or series changes. The
# in-app setup panel also has a field for this - only set it here if you're using options 1/2 above.
VIMEO_SHOWCASE_IDS=

# Publishing to SoundCloud is also entirely optional, and needs an Artist-Pro SoundCloud account.
#
# NORMAL SETUP: same story as Vimeo above - open the app itself and use the "Set up SoundCloud
# publishing…" panel (next to the save-path fields), which walks through registering an app at
# developers.soundcloud.com and saves everything to data/soundcloud-app-config.json instead. The
# SOUNDCLOUD_* variables below are an advanced/optional override for anyone who'd rather manage it
# as env vars (e.g. a scripted install) - if set, they take priority over the in-app panel and
# lock its fields. Leave them all blank unless you specifically want that.
#
# The Client ID and Client Secret from the same app page as above - either way (this file or the
# in-app panel), a one-time browser sign-in is still needed afterward via the "Connect to
# SoundCloud" button in the app.
SOUNDCLOUD_CLIENT_ID=
SOUNDCLOUD_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Only needed if the app isn't reachable at http://localhost:3000 (e.g. a different port) - must
# exactly match the redirect URI registered with the SoundCloud app.
SOUNDCLOUD_REDIRECT_URI=

# Comma-separated numeric playlist IDs every published track gets added to, e.g. the current
# year's sermons and the current sermon series. A playlist's ordinary web link doesn't show this
# ID - easiest way to find it is the in-app setup panel's "Add by link" box, even if you're
# otherwise managing everything else here via env vars. The in-app setup panel
# also has a field for this - only set it here if you're using the env vars above.
SOUNDCLOUD_PLAYLIST_IDS=
